# Copy to .env IN THIS DIRECTORY (repo root) and fill in. NEVER commit real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file is TRACKED BY GIT — it must only ever contain empty placeholders.
# Put real values in .env, which is gitignored.
#
# `node --env-file=.env ...` resolves the path relative to the directory you run
# it from, so run the demo from the repo root.

# Blockfrost project ID for the network you are targeting. The demo-vault is
# wired to PREVIEW (examples/demo-vault/app/src/deposit.ts), so this must be a
# Preview project — a Preprod or Mainnet key will fail against the Preview URL.
BLOCKFROST_API_KEY=

# Seed phrase of the wallet that deploys the gate and uses the vault. For the
# demo this is one wallet doing both jobs, so on PREVIEW it must:
#   - hold >= 1 AdaLinkPlatformAuth token
#     (policy 31485bcbe7184757c9a8b8526bc79672671f12466ed8880c42b344b5)
#   - have ~15 test ADA: 2 stake-registration deposit + ~4.4 min-ADA for the
#     published reference script + 5 demo deposit + fees
#   - have MORE THAN ONE UTxO. withGate adds the token's UTxO as a reference
#     input, and evolution-sdk excludes reference inputs from coin selection —
#     a single combined UTxO leaves nothing to pay fees with.
# Use a throwaway testnet wallet. This key can move every asset it holds.
WALLET_MNEMONIC=
